Decisions (mine): (12) No session title at all; a per-run unique title is not safe either (resolve_session_by_title prefers '<title> #N'). Cost: the child gets Hermes' automatic title. (13) Empty effective set beyond the own toolset ⇒ tools.show must show exactly the own tools by name and a total equal to the listed count — the only independent signal against the fail-open inventory; there is no reply field marking fail-open. (14) A describe refusal other than -32601 never refuses the run: no claim, note, retry next poll / other window. (15) Reconnect detection = gateway.ready + gateway state ≠ open (primary socket only); any bump ⇒ explicit resume before the next submit. (16) Reconciling at submit_requested submits only into a lazy session with no pending/running admission; an own pending admission is adopted; otherwise unknown/submit_unconfirmed. Trade-off: a lost reply whose admission is already terminal now ends unknown instead of recovering through an idempotent resubmit. Before the first send in a drive, an unclear re-attach snapshot is a refusal (toolsets_not_checkable), since nothing of ours was sent. A resume failure once a submit may have been sent → unknown, not refused. (17) prompt.submit now runs its own repeat loop (same REPEATS/backoff/5001 rule as rpcRepeat) so the epoch is checked before each attempt. (18) Schema: read-check per open instead of a per-path process cache — a cache would hide a newer schema written by another process (test_a_newer_schema_is_refused).
